"Team,\n\nBottom line: CrowdStrike’s October 2026 demand signal remains positive. Net Score was 37.14, up 0.69 points versus July 2026 and 10.54 points versus October 2025. Pervasion rose to 40.90.\n\nWhat changed: Sequential Net Score movement was modest, while the year-over-year recovery was materially larger. Q/Q and Y/Y Z-Scores were 0.129 and 0.892; the raw values are available, but approved interpretation bands remain Source Needed.\n\nResearch implication: The evidence supports continued recovery and broader deployment, with selective enterprise strength and geographic divergence. It does not validate a causal or predictive relationship to Net New ARR.\n\nReview requested: Please approve, revise, or reject SIG-02 and the proposed SIG-02 → KPI-003 bridge. We also need cohort/regional Ns, current retention, current shared-account data, and approved Z-Score methodology bands.\n\nEvidence: ETR-OCT26-NS; ETR-OCT26-PV; ETR-OCT26-ZS; ETR-OCT26-G2K; ETR-OCT26-F500; ETR-OCT26-LARGE.\n\nHuman Review Required.",
